 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Large kitchen equipment are big appliances and fittings that usually stay in one place.\n• Cooker (stove): gas, electric, kerosene or charcoal; with burners (hobs or rings), an oven and a grill. Used for boiling, frying, baking and grilling.\n• Refrigerator (fridge): keeps food cool (about 0–5 °C) to slow the growth of germs; it has a freezer box, shelves, a vegetable drawer and door racks.\n• Freezer: keeps food frozen (about −18 °C) for weeks or months: meat, fish, ice.\n• Dishwasher: washes, rinses and dries plates and pots with hot water and detergent.\n• Sink, cupboards and worktops are large fittings.\nMost large equipment use electricity or gas, so they must be used safely.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "f": "fresh fish for two months"
  },
  "problem": "Which large equipment is best to keep {f}, and why?",
  "steps": [
   "A fridge keeps food cool for only a few days.",
   "A freezer keeps it frozen at about −{18} °C, so germs cannot grow for months."
  ],
  "answer": "A freezer.",
  "checks": []
 },
